<<~ ahu slot=`#/head`>>

! Problems ~ a refusal reaches the editor

The files the house writes serve the operator as a surface they edit, the tideline ruling's seam. A refusal the door names (a torn frame, a stale seal, a body fault) MUST reach the place the operator edits, so the door speaks a line any editor's problem matcher reads, and a `tasks.json` matcher carries it into VS Code's Problems panel with no extension in the loop. The extension upgrade waits.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/the-shape`>>

!! The shape

```text
path:line:col: severity: code: message
```

* ''One line per diagnostic.'' `lares meme check --format=problems <file.mem ...>` prints each finding once, in the order the files stand named; a file with no finding prints nothing, and the human lines fall silent. A message holding a newline folds onto one line.
* ''Positions count from 1 against the file's own text'', as it sits on disk, never the text normalize would leave; the column counts UTF-16 code units, the unit the editor reads. A finding no one mark places (a stage fault, a flag, a frame drift) reads `path:1:1`.
* ''Severity follows the gate.'' A finding that makes the read-alone seat exit 1 reads `error`; an advisory reading the gate passes (a flag, an unbound head, bare data) reads `warning`; a grammar preference, never a fault, reads `info`.
* ''The exit stays the human seat's'': `0` canonical, `1` any drift or fault, `2` usage. `--format` names `problems` alone and refuses any other value; it reads the normalize law alone, so it refuses beside `--gradient`, `--edges` or `--sitting`, and `lares meme normalize` takes no `--format`.
* ''The unnamed-dirty reading stays human.'' It names files nobody named, so the problems shape never asks git for it.

!!! The codes

```text
no-etx · second-stx · second-etx · second-soh · etx-before-stx · eot-out-of-order
meta-before-stx · head-meta-split · retired-trailer · torn-spelling   (a torn frame, error)
stale-bcc · unchecked · restamp · drift                                (a seal or frame drift, error)
duplicate-meta-key · stage · post-eot                                  (a body or boundary fault, error)
flag · head-unbound · bare                                             (advisory, warning)
grammar                                                                (a preference, info)
```

A torn frame places at the mark its kind names: `no-etx` at STX, a second mark at that mark, `head-meta-split` at the root meta fence, `meta-before-stx` at the stray fence. `stale-bcc` places at the `bcc=` run inside the ETX mark, `duplicate-meta-key` at the key's second line, `post-eot` at the first foreign byte past EOT, `head-unbound` at the head. `torn-spelling` names no single mark and reads `path:1:1`.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/the-matcher`>>

!! The matcher

Drop this into the workspace's `.vscode/tasks.json` and run the task over the open carrier; each line lands in the Problems panel at its line and column. The regexp reads the path lazily, so a Windows drive letter keeps its colon inside the path.

```json tasks
{
  "version": "2.0.0",
  "tasks": [
    {
      "label": "lares: check this meme",
      "type": "shell",
      "command": "lares meme check --format=problems \"${relativeFile}\"",
      "options": { "cwd": "${workspaceFolder}" },
      "presentation": { "reveal": "silent", "clear": true },
      "problemMatcher": {
        "owner": "lares",
        "source": "lares meme check",
        "fileLocation": ["relative", "${workspaceFolder}"],
        "pattern": {
          "regexp": "^(.+?):(\\d+):(\\d+): (error|warning|info): ([^:\\s]+): (.*)$",
          "file": 1,
          "line": 2,
          "column": 3,
          "severity": 4,
          "code": 5,
          "message": 6
        }
      }
    }
  ]
}
```

* ''A wider sweep'' keeps the same matcher and names more files: `lares meme check --format=problems $(git ls-files '*.mem')` reads every tracked carrier.
* ''The regexp stands welded'': `packages/lares-cli/tests/meme-check-problems-matcher.test.ts` reads this fence, holds its regexp equal to the door's own (`packages/lares-cli/src/problems.ts`), and parses every golden line through it, so the shape, the door and this sample move together or red.
* ''Later doors share the shape.'' `lares surface log --follow` and the stand-off and skip readings of the watch core speak the same line when they land, under the same matcher.

<<~/ahu>>

